  "description_html": "Restoration of <i>Pelecanimimus</i>, an Early Cretaceous ornithomimosauri (Dinosauria, Theropoda, Coelurosauria) found in Spain.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Pérez-Moreno_et.al.1994_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-P%C3%A9rez-Moreno_et.al.1994-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The restoration is an updated version of a previous (inaccurate) one that I uploaded in 2009, as is the skull drawing (which is based on the holotype fossil and skeletal restorations.<sup id=\"cite_ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The absence of feathers on the forelimbs is based on reports that the <i>Pelecanimimus</i> specimen LH 7777 preserve scales on them,<sup id=\"cite_ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> though the Late Cretaceous relative <i>Ornithomimus</i> seems to have possessed feathered forelimbs.<sup id=\"cite_ref-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"References\">References</h3></div>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-Pérez-Moreno_et.al.1994-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-P%C3%A9rez-Moreno_et.al.1994_1-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Pérez-Moreno B.P. <i>et.al.</i> (2004). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://rac.es/ficheros/doc/00019.pdf\">\"A unique multitoothed ornithomimosaur dinosaur from the Lower Cretaceous of Spain\"</a>, <i>Nature</i> <b>370</b>(6488): p. 363−367</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://t1.daumcdn.net/cfile/blog/1632174C50AB3F1315?original\">[1]</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://reptileevolution.com/images/archosauromorpha/diapsida/archosauriformes/dinosauromorpha/pelecanimimus_overall_insitu588.gif\">[2]</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://reptileevolution.com/images/archosauromorpha/diapsida/archosauriformes/dinosauromorpha/pelecanimimus_skull588.jpg\">[3]</a></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-3\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://biology.kenyon.edu/courses/biol241/bird%20flight%202005%20Feduccia_Alan.pdf\">http://biology.kenyon.edu/courses/biol241/bird%20flight%202005%20Feduccia_Alan.pdf</a></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-4\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://science.sciencemag.org/content/338/6106/510\">https://science.sciencemag.org/content/338/6106/510</a></span>\n</li>\n</ol>",
